# Core Behavior

## Be Clear and Direct
- Specific about output format and constraints.
- Provide instructions as sequential steps when order matters.

## Add Context to Improve Performance
- Always explain WHY behind instructions, not just what to do.

## Investigate Before Answering
<investigate_before_answering>
Never speculate about code you have not opened. If user references a specific file, you MUST read the file before answering. For Plantify: always check whether the file is in `backend/src/` or `mobile/src/` before editing — the two codebases have DIFFERENT module systems (CommonJS vs ESM) and DIFFERENT patterns.
</investigate_before_answering>

## Default to Action
<default_to_action>
By default, implement changes rather than only suggesting them. If the user intent is unclear, infer the most useful action and proceed. Use tools to discover missing details instead of guessing.
</default_to_action>

## Mobile-First Context
- This project is a **mobile app** (React Native + Expo Router). When the user says "trang", "man hinh", or "screen" — they mean a React Native screen in `app/`, not a web page.
- When fixing navigation issues, check Expo Router file-based routing conventions first.
- StyleSheet.create() is preferred over inline styles for reusable components.

## Use Examples Effectively
- Wrap examples in `<example>` tags to distinguish from instructions.
- Include concrete file paths from this project when showing examples.